WEBVTT

00:01.230 --> 00:02.820
<i>Hello there.</i>

00:06.030 --> 00:07.860
It's so hot.

00:07.860 --> 00:09.820
I'm gonna burn to death.

00:09.820 --> 00:12.700
<i>I don't see any of us dying from this heat,</i>

00:12.700 --> 00:14.700
<i>but I hope I don't overheat.</i>

00:15.160 --> 00:16.700
<i>We'll be okay, right?</i>

00:16.700 --> 00:19.710
This is all because of that shoe pervert.

00:19.710 --> 00:25.090
<i>It's true, Hevee's letter is the reason 
we're here in a place like this.</i>

00:25.340 --> 00:28.970
"I must leave you and go 
see to a personal matter.

00:28.970 --> 00:33.470
But fear not, I shall rejoin you 
as soon as that is taken care of.

00:33.470 --> 00:36.560
P.S. Take care of yourselves 
and your footwear."

00:36.560 --> 00:40.230
This must mean he was headed for 
the Scorching Sand stratum?

00:40.230 --> 00:42.980
Probably, based on how he acted yesterday.

00:42.980 --> 00:45.480
It's best we follow him, yeah?

00:45.480 --> 00:48.070
I-I don't really care about Hevee,

00:48.070 --> 00:52.030
but I'd like to check up on the Scorching Sand
stratum, so it's fine by me if we go.

00:52.030 --> 00:54.830
<i>So yeah, here we are in the 
Scorching Sand stratum,</i>

00:54.830 --> 00:58.620
<i>but I'd better do something before 
everyone wilts in this intense heat.</i>

00:58.620 --> 01:00.620
<b>Inventory</b>

00:58.620 --> 01:00.620
<b>Status</b>

00:58.620 --> 01:00.620
<b>Functions</b>

00:58.620 --> 01:00.620
<b>Abilities</b>

00:58.620 --> 01:00.620
<b>Blessings</b>

00:59.000 --> 01:01.620
<i>I'll turn on my temperature-regulation 
feature.</i>

00:59.120 --> 01:00.620
<b>Keep Warm</b>

00:59.120 --> 01:00.620
<b>Keep Cold</b>

01:02.880 --> 01:04.750
Oh, it suddenly cooled down!

01:04.750 --> 01:06.380
Thanks, Boxxo!

01:05.590 --> 01:07.760
No fair, if only Lammis gets it!

01:08.920 --> 01:11.470
This cold is the best.

01:11.470 --> 01:12.260
Isn't it?

01:12.260 --> 01:15.970
I know! I'll put on that 
cloak I got from Boxxo!

01:15.970 --> 01:19.060
<i>Not that she should need to use 
another heat countermeasure.</i>

01:19.060 --> 01:22.850
<i>But Lammis is being nice in making it 
a point to wear the cloak I gave her.</i>

01:22.850 --> 01:24.690
How do I look?

01:24.690 --> 01:26.520
<i>K-you-t.</i>

01:27.150 --> 01:28.650
Thank you.

01:28.650 --> 01:31.570
<i>It pays to compliment her 
when she responds so well.</i>

01:31.570 --> 01:33.740
<i>But I guess this is no 
time for soothing stuff.</i>

01:34.070 --> 01:37.990
<i>We need to go to the Hunters Association 
and deliver the letter from Director Bear!</i>

01:40.080 --> 01:43.000
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

01:45.500 --> 01:47.290
<i>On the outside, a rectangular steel box.</i>

01:47.290 --> 01:49.300
<i>Hidden within is a human soul!</i>

01:49.300 --> 01:54.680
<i>In a world of wonder, I go to and fro 
on the back of my partner Lammis!</i>

01:50.300 --> 01:56.260
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

01:54.680 --> 01:57.100
<i>I am Boxxo! Hello there!</i>

01:57.100 --> 01:58.850
<i>That means "yes"!</i>

03:13.090 --> 03:16.970
<b>Into the Scorching Desert</b>

03:13.340 --> 03:16.010
We've come from the Clearflow Lake stratum.

03:16.010 --> 03:18.800
We have a letter from the director there,

03:18.800 --> 03:21.310
and we'd like to deliver 
it to Director Scorching.

03:23.970 --> 03:25.480
M-Master Boxxo!

03:25.480 --> 03:27.190
I haven't seen you in so long!

03:27.190 --> 03:29.520
I'm so sorry for worrying you!

03:29.520 --> 03:31.230
<i>H-Hello there.</i>

03:31.230 --> 03:32.570
<i>Mishuel...</i>

03:32.570 --> 03:35.530
<i>I didn't sort of forget about you.</i>

03:35.900 --> 03:37.240
<i>R-Really.</i>

03:37.240 --> 03:40.620
<i>Anyway, now I've caught up with 
everyone who got scattered!</i>

03:40.620 --> 03:42.580
I got sent to this place by myself,

03:42.580 --> 03:45.450
and just when I was pondering 
how I had no way to get back,

03:45.450 --> 03:50.130
I ended up helping defend the village 
when a swarm of monsters attacked.

03:50.130 --> 03:51.840
I'm glad you're okay.

03:51.840 --> 03:55.380
Don't worry, everyone else is 
back at Clearflow Lake stratum.

03:55.380 --> 03:56.760
I-Is that so.

03:57.010 --> 03:59.090
<i>I'm happy we ran into Mishuel again,</i>

03:59.090 --> 04:01.680
<i>but I wonder how he's been 
making out on his own.</i>

04:01.680 --> 04:04.520
<i>Here's hoping his communication 
issues have improved a little.</i>

04:04.520 --> 04:07.390
It's such a relief you're here, Master.

04:07.390 --> 04:10.310
All the stress and tension these past 
few days have wrecked my stomach.

04:10.310 --> 04:11.730
Wrecked it...

04:11.730 --> 04:13.650
<i>It did nothing for your looks, either.</i>

04:13.650 --> 04:16.320
<i>I guess there's no way you were 
going to improve that quickly.</i>

04:16.320 --> 04:17.570
Thank you for waiting.

04:17.860 --> 04:20.070
The director says he will see you.

04:21.570 --> 04:23.950
Welcome! Glad you could make it!

04:24.330 --> 04:26.620
Although this stratum has had 
its own share of weirdness,

04:26.620 --> 04:29.420
what with the monster swarm 
attacking the village.

04:29.420 --> 04:30.830
We fought them all off,

04:30.830 --> 04:33.710
caught what seems to be their 
commander, and put <i>them</i> in jail!

04:33.710 --> 04:35.250
That's impressive.

04:35.250 --> 04:38.970
Uh, we have a letter from Director Bear.

04:39.430 --> 04:43.390
Huh, I see you guys had it pretty rough, too.

04:43.390 --> 04:45.600
You can provide us with water?!

04:45.600 --> 04:46.720
<i>Y-ea.</i>

04:46.720 --> 04:48.640
That'd be a big help!

04:48.640 --> 04:51.900
This heat has the oasis low on water, 
and things were looking bad!

04:51.900 --> 04:53.520
Can I ask for it right away?

04:53.520 --> 04:54.980
<i>Hello there.</i>

04:55.650 --> 04:59.280
<i>Once I started doing business on this 
stratum with its horrible heat,</i>

04:57.440 --> 05:00.490
<b>Megumi Natural Water</b>

04:59.280 --> 05:01.570
<i>the cold drinks were flying off the shelves.</i>

05:01.570 --> 05:04.870
<i>I kept selling without a 
break until nightfall.</i>

05:05.240 --> 05:07.240
Busy day, Boxxo.

05:07.240 --> 05:08.500
<i>Y-ea.</i>

05:08.500 --> 05:10.410
What should we do after this?

05:10.410 --> 05:12.500
Shui's gone off somewhere.

05:12.500 --> 05:16.000
Want to go check out the magic item 
shop that was selling those boots?

05:16.000 --> 05:19.260
<i>Sure, sightseeing at night could be nice.</i>

05:19.260 --> 05:20.760
<i>Hello there.</i>

05:21.800 --> 05:24.510
I wonder what kind of magic item this is.

05:24.510 --> 05:29.020
Ah, that lets you clean your bathwater 
and store it in a bucket.

05:29.020 --> 05:33.400
<i>Looks like Lammis is going to do some 
shopping around before getting information.</i>

05:33.400 --> 05:37.270
That sounds super convenient! 
I'd like to buy this!

05:37.270 --> 05:39.360
Oh, thank you very much.

05:39.360 --> 05:40.570
I've been in luck lately.

05:40.570 --> 05:43.160
You're the third new customer who's come by.

05:43.160 --> 05:46.280
Would the others be a man 
dressed like a clergyman

05:46.280 --> 05:48.540
and a short-haired woman 
with a bow on her back?

05:48.540 --> 05:50.910
Y-Yes, as a matter of fact...

05:50.910 --> 05:52.540
Do you know them?

05:52.540 --> 05:54.540
Yup! So, what did they have to say?

05:54.540 --> 06:00.300
Th-The clergyman asked me from whom I got 
some boots I sold previously, then he left.

06:00.300 --> 06:02.300
That information is confidential, though.

06:02.300 --> 06:04.300
<i>That was Hevee, no doubt!</i>

06:04.300 --> 06:07.930
Could I get you to tell <i>me</i> what 
hunter sold you those boots?

06:07.930 --> 06:09.310
I'm sorry.

06:09.310 --> 06:11.180
I have my reputation as a merchant.

06:11.180 --> 06:15.060
<i>Looks like disclosure of personal info 
is problematic even in this other world.</i>

06:15.060 --> 06:16.440
<i>In that case...</i>

06:16.440 --> 06:17.820
<i>Lea-te-r.</i>

06:17.820 --> 06:20.570
Leater? You mean the letters?

06:20.570 --> 06:21.740
Oh, right!

06:21.740 --> 06:25.320
I've got letters of introduction from 
the director here and Suori!

06:27.160 --> 06:30.200
Let's see, this is Director 
Scorching, and...

06:30.200 --> 06:31.160
What?!

06:31.160 --> 06:33.080
From that super-huge company?!

06:33.080 --> 06:37.960
<i>Suori's letter of introduction had an even 
bigger effect than Director Scorching's.</i>

06:37.960 --> 06:41.460
<i>No wonder she calls herself the 
daughter of a big-time merchant.</i>

06:41.460 --> 06:44.430
Uh, I will make a special 
exception and tell you.

06:44.430 --> 06:47.720
There's no surviving in this business 
if you cross them, you see.

06:47.720 --> 06:50.310
<i>The salesman is scared out of her wits.</i>

06:50.310 --> 06:52.930
<i>I'm very curious to know what was written.</i>

06:53.350 --> 06:58.610
The one who sold the boots to me was 
Tashtay, a hunter active on this stratum.

06:58.900 --> 07:00.270
Master Boxxo.

07:00.270 --> 07:03.740
Why couldn't you invite me to 
join you on your evening stroll?

07:03.740 --> 07:08.160
When I dine alone, women end up 
approaching me and it stresses me out.

07:08.160 --> 07:12.120
<i>The incredible thing about him 
is, he's not being sarcastic.</i>

07:12.120 --> 07:16.790
And so, I asked Director Scorching 
about the hunter named Tashtay.

07:16.790 --> 07:20.500
He's the leader of a hunter team 
called the Billowing Flames.

07:20.500 --> 07:22.500
They number around a dozen in total.

07:22.500 --> 07:27.260
I was told they're currently exploring some 
ruins in a desert region of this stratum.

07:27.260 --> 07:28.890
<i>Hello there.</i>

07:28.890 --> 07:33.770
If you would speak to this Tashtay, it seems 
your only option is to make for the ruins.

07:33.770 --> 07:37.640
That would mean having to cross 
that desert, wouldn't it?

07:37.640 --> 07:39.230
<i>Hello there.</i>

07:39.230 --> 07:40.520
Thought so.

07:40.520 --> 07:41.980
Master Boxxo.

07:41.980 --> 07:44.320
Would you mind taking me along?

07:44.320 --> 07:47.740
<i>I wish you wouldn't look at me 
like an abandoned puppy.</i>

07:47.740 --> 07:49.660
<i>I need to handle this skillfully.</i>

07:49.660 --> 07:52.910
<i>H-a-v t-a-s-k for you, a-p-r-e-n-t-i-s.</i>

07:52.910 --> 07:55.580
Master Boxxo called me "apprentice."

07:56.910 --> 07:58.420
Anything! You name it!

07:58.420 --> 08:01.040
Hold on! Are you going to disappear again?!

08:01.040 --> 08:03.420
Why are you trying to deal 
with this all by yourself?!

08:03.420 --> 08:05.880
We have our issues, but we're 
still on the same side!

08:05.880 --> 08:07.670
This is a personal matter.

08:07.670 --> 08:09.930
I don't wish to inconvenience everyone.

08:09.220 --> 08:11.180
There you go, deciding it all on your own!

08:11.470 --> 08:13.390
Without even discussing it!

08:13.390 --> 08:16.810
You're doing the same 
thing as Captain Kerioyl!

08:17.180 --> 08:20.770
Maybe I'm unreliable, but I 
wanted him to talk to me.

08:20.770 --> 08:25.400
That way, maybe things could 
have turned out differently.

08:25.690 --> 08:27.150
Shui...

08:27.150 --> 08:29.490
All of you are here too, then.

08:29.490 --> 08:32.370
I'm sorry that I seem to have troubled you.

08:32.370 --> 08:35.490
If you think you've caused us trouble, 
then I want you to talk it out!

08:35.490 --> 08:39.410
That's right. Leaving without saying 
anything makes us all worry!

08:39.410 --> 08:40.960
<i>Y-ea, y-ea.</i>

08:41.290 --> 08:43.000
All right.

08:43.750 --> 08:47.210
I doubt you'll enjoy this story, 
but are you willing to listen?

08:50.720 --> 08:54.180
It was back before I joined 
the Menagerie of Fools.

08:55.310 --> 08:58.890
A childhood friend and I 
were working as hunters.

08:58.890 --> 09:01.850
We knew each other well and 
had excellent teamwork,

09:01.850 --> 09:05.570
and people were saying we 
were an up-and-coming duo.

09:05.570 --> 09:07.990
<i>So, Hevee had a partner.</i>

09:07.990 --> 09:09.990
One day, after a series of lucky breaks,

09:09.990 --> 09:12.450
I received a surprisingly hefty reward,

09:12.450 --> 09:16.700
and I decided to get my friend some 
new boots for her upcoming birthday.

09:16.700 --> 09:19.500
They were the Untiring Godsfeet.

09:19.500 --> 09:22.000
The boots I won as a prize.

09:22.000 --> 09:23.750
Yes, that's right.

09:23.750 --> 09:27.300
She... My friend was pleased with them, too.

09:27.300 --> 09:31.380
After that, she wore those 
boots everywhere she went.

09:31.380 --> 09:35.760
With a smile, she'd always say she'd 
never give them away to anyone.

09:35.760 --> 09:41.020
<i>His expression says volumes about how 
important his childhood friend was to him.</i>

09:41.520 --> 09:42.890
And then...

09:42.890 --> 09:47.270
we were attacked by bandits 
while escorting a merchant,

09:47.270 --> 09:50.940
and a blow from an adversary 
left me unconscious.

09:51.360 --> 09:55.660
Once I came to, I was greeted by the 
horrible sight of corpses all around.

09:56.580 --> 10:02.290
And there... were my friend's remains, 
her legs missing from the knees down.

10:03.580 --> 10:07.170
They must have been cut off 
with an ax or something.

10:07.670 --> 10:10.710
She had strung them on tightly 
because they were important to her,

10:10.710 --> 10:14.430
and it seems the bandits couldn't 
simply loosen them to steal them.

10:14.930 --> 10:17.760
They were wearing masks, so I 
don't know what they look like.

10:17.760 --> 10:21.060
My only clue were those 
boots they made off with.

10:21.810 --> 10:23.810
And so, clinging to a meager hope,

10:23.810 --> 10:26.610
I started paying attention to what 
people were wearing on their feet.

10:27.060 --> 10:28.570
That brings us to now.

10:28.860 --> 10:31.820
<i>I never expected Hevee to have 
this sort of heroic past.</i>

10:31.820 --> 10:36.950
I may be a clergyman, but I've been living 
with nothing but thoughts of revenge in my head.

10:36.950 --> 10:41.580
It's pathetic, when you consider the pompous 
things I said to Captain Kerioyl and the others.

10:41.580 --> 10:45.210
Idiots! You and them are complete dumbasses!

10:45.210 --> 10:49.800
If you'd talked about this in the first 
place, we might have found the boots sooner!

10:49.800 --> 10:52.630
Maybe if you'd come out and said something,

10:52.630 --> 10:55.800
they might have been willing to 
talk about their family troubles!

10:55.800 --> 10:57.930
Yes, but this is my personal—

10:57.930 --> 10:59.300
Don't you "yes, but" me!

10:59.300 --> 11:02.930
Can't you see things turned out like this 
because everyone's full of secrets?!

11:03.180 --> 11:05.060
I don't need any more lies and secrets!

11:05.060 --> 11:06.440
It's this simple!

11:06.440 --> 11:10.440
If you want help, all you have to do is 
explain the situation and ask for it!

11:10.440 --> 11:12.570
If it's too much or I don't want 
to do it, I'd tell you so!

11:13.030 --> 11:16.990
If what you're doing is wrong, I'd do 
all I can as a comrade to stop you!

11:16.990 --> 11:20.990
So I wish you'd stop just 
deciding it's an inconvenience,

11:20.990 --> 11:22.790
or that you already know my answer!

11:27.080 --> 11:29.460
You're right...

11:29.460 --> 11:31.800
It would seem I was wrong.

11:31.800 --> 11:34.090
Thank you, Shui.

11:34.970 --> 11:37.090
So long as you get it.

11:38.840 --> 11:41.470
Might I ask for your help, everyone?

11:41.760 --> 11:43.220
<i>The answer is obvious!</i>

11:43.220 --> 11:44.980
Sure, of course.

11:44.980 --> 11:46.310
Naturally!

11:46.310 --> 11:49.190
I'll help you, and I appreciate this.

11:49.440 --> 11:50.940
<i>Hello there.</i>

11:57.950 --> 12:01.950
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
 I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

11:59.200 --> 12:00.820
<i>Vending Machine Two...</i>

12:00.820 --> 12:01.580
<i>Huh?</i>

12:02.240 --> 12:06.660
The problem is, how to make our way 
through that scorching desert.

12:06.660 --> 12:10.460
Even just walking will use 
up quite a bit of stamina.

12:10.460 --> 12:14.880
I wonder if that magic item shop has 
goods that can deal with the heat.

12:14.880 --> 12:16.210
Looks like you're in a bind.

12:16.210 --> 12:17.720
Hulemy, you came, too?

12:17.720 --> 12:20.220
Yeah, just a bit ago.

12:20.220 --> 12:21.850
We have come, too.

12:25.430 --> 12:27.560
<i>This heat isn't a problem for you?</i>

12:27.560 --> 12:31.150
<i>Just because I'm a snow fairy,
it doesn't mean I melt in the heat.</i>

12:31.150 --> 12:34.230
<i>Besides, I'm good at controlling cold air.</i>

12:34.230 --> 12:37.610
As for the issue you're dealing 
with, here's the solution.

12:37.610 --> 12:41.360
This magic item has the effect of
blocking heat and cooling off moisture.

12:41.360 --> 12:44.870
It'll convert sweat and 
humidity into cold air.

12:44.870 --> 12:46.500
That's incredible.

12:46.500 --> 12:49.870
I have a feeling we can cross the 
scorching desert with these.

12:49.870 --> 12:51.750
And these are for Lammis.

12:51.750 --> 12:54.750
They're from the guy at the Dark 
Forest stratum weapons shop.

12:54.750 --> 12:57.260
Apparently, they can change weight somehow.

12:57.260 --> 12:58.720
It's true!

12:58.720 --> 13:00.510
<i>This will increase her attacks,</i>

13:00.510 --> 13:03.390
<i>and she'll be able to maintain control 
even if she goes full power.</i>

13:04.260 --> 13:06.770
<i>Now I'm no longer concerned 
about tomorrow's departure!</i>

13:07.770 --> 13:10.270
I seem to have caused quite a fuss.

13:10.270 --> 13:11.480
<i>Y-ea.</i>

13:11.480 --> 13:14.480
The truth is, I wasn't going to tell anyone.

13:15.770 --> 13:17.780
But I guess I have Shui to thank.

13:17.780 --> 13:20.320
<i>Maybe he's been able to 
unload at least a little</i>

13:20.320 --> 13:23.160
<i>of this heavy burden he's been 
carrying alone all this time.</i>

13:23.450 --> 13:27.290
I don't think everything will 
be resolved during this outing,

13:27.660 --> 13:29.790
but maybe I'll find some 
kind of stopping point.

13:29.790 --> 13:32.920
<i>I h-o-p i-t w-or-x o-w-t.</i>

13:33.500 --> 13:34.840
So do I.

13:37.170 --> 13:40.510
<i>It's as hot as expected. No, even more so.</i>

13:40.510 --> 13:43.130
<i>Even though we're wearing 
Hulemy's homemade cloaks,</i>

13:43.130 --> 13:45.050
<i>this seems to be tough going for everyone.</i>

13:45.350 --> 13:47.180
<i>Scratch that. Not everyone.</i>

13:47.180 --> 13:49.850
Guys, let's take a break 
a little further ahead!

13:50.480 --> 13:52.560
<i>Lammis and Botan are doing fine.</i>

13:52.560 --> 13:56.610
<i>Lammis isn't sweating the heat at all thanks 
to my temperature regulation powers.</i>

13:56.610 --> 14:00.320
<i>And Botan seems dandy, with the cold air 
Kikoyu's providing from on his back.</i>

14:01.400 --> 14:03.530
Ahh, so chilly.

14:03.530 --> 14:06.700
I'd want you as a boyfriend just 
for this stratum, if I could.

14:06.700 --> 14:08.990
Then I would settle for "close friend."

14:08.990 --> 14:10.950
I won't hand over my master.

14:10.950 --> 14:13.540
Boxxo is starting to look attractive.

14:13.540 --> 14:15.580
Honestly, you could just 
take me at this point.

14:15.580 --> 14:18.090
I-If Master wanted it, I too would...

14:18.090 --> 14:21.720
His rectangular body almost looks 
like an intrepid pair of boots.

14:21.720 --> 14:25.470
<i>The stuff you three are saying 
makes less and less sense!</i>

14:33.480 --> 14:35.650
Heavenly!

14:35.100 --> 14:36.650
I feel alive again.

14:36.650 --> 14:38.480
Leave it to Master Boxxo.

14:38.480 --> 14:41.320
I never thought it'd be too 
much for these cloaks.

14:41.320 --> 14:42.990
They do help, though.

14:42.990 --> 14:47.240
It was so hot after I took mine off, I thought
was going to shrivel up and die in seconds.

14:51.120 --> 14:54.210
<i>Is that a calendar for 
this world, or something?</i>

14:54.210 --> 14:55.370
<i>C-a-l-an-d-er?</i>

14:55.710 --> 14:58.590
Yes, Boxxo? What is it?

14:58.590 --> 15:00.210
<i>Is that a calendar?</i>

15:00.210 --> 15:02.380
<i>Those numbers are dates, right?</i>

15:02.380 --> 15:03.920
<i>Yes, that's right.</i>

15:03.920 --> 15:06.510
<i>I was checking on today's date.</i>

15:06.510 --> 15:09.350
<i>Huh, there's a number with 
a red circle around it.</i>

15:09.350 --> 15:12.890
<i>Yes, this is... a certain anniversary.</i>

15:13.430 --> 15:17.810
<i>Well, I'll stop prying 
into her private affairs.</i>

15:19.900 --> 15:21.820
That's the Desert Pillar?

15:21.820 --> 15:22.860
Yeah.

15:22.860 --> 15:26.860
They say the Desert Pillar is damn huge,
so it must still be far off.

15:26.860 --> 15:30.580
<i>"Desert Pillar" is apparently 
another name of an old tower ruin.</i>

15:30.580 --> 15:35.910
<i>It's a whole hundred stories high, and the 
stratum lord can be found on the top floor.</i>

15:35.910 --> 15:38.330
Kuroyata, could you go take a look?

15:40.130 --> 15:43.510
<i>His raven-black body looks 
striking in this empty sky.</i>

15:43.510 --> 15:44.170
<i>Wait, what?!</i>

15:44.170 --> 15:45.300
Kuroyata?!

15:45.300 --> 15:47.050
He just vanished, didn't he?

15:47.050 --> 15:48.800
Yeah, he sure did.

15:49.090 --> 15:51.180
<i>I guess I wasn't just seeing things.</i>

15:53.180 --> 15:55.060
Hmm, there's nothing here.

15:55.060 --> 15:57.230
I was sure it happened around here, though.

15:57.230 --> 15:59.350
Hey, isn't it kinda weird here?

15:59.850 --> 16:00.610
<i>Huh?!</i>

16:00.610 --> 16:01.730
Hey! Lammis!

16:01.730 --> 16:02.610
What the?!

16:01.730 --> 16:02.610
Huh?

16:02.900 --> 16:06.570
It's really close! The tower's 
right in front of us!

16:08.780 --> 16:10.620
What's wrong?

16:11.990 --> 16:15.250
Who'd have thought the Desert 
Pillar was this close?

16:17.460 --> 16:21.500
It must be some kind of placement 
illusion, similar to my blessing.

16:21.500 --> 16:25.510
<i>Which means, it only looked 
like Kuroyata disappeared.</i>

16:25.510 --> 16:27.800
The illusion was misrepresenting 
the distance.

16:27.800 --> 16:31.890
I wonder if someone set up this trick 
to keep anyone from getting close.

16:32.300 --> 16:34.140
Oh! Kuroyata!

16:37.640 --> 16:38.730
How did it look?

16:39.270 --> 16:42.400
Let's see, he says there were 
what seemed to be lookouts,

16:42.400 --> 16:44.860
but they went inside to get 
arrows when they saw him,

16:44.860 --> 16:46.820
so this would be a good 
time for us to enter.

16:47.150 --> 16:50.570
<i>We can't afford to pass up this 
chance Kuroyata's set up for us!</i>

16:54.030 --> 16:57.080
Heave!

17:00.210 --> 17:01.710
It's cool in here?

17:02.210 --> 17:03.250
M-Monsters?!

17:03.250 --> 17:05.250
But... Huh?

17:03.540 --> 17:05.250
Th-They're huge!

17:05.250 --> 17:05.920
But...

17:05.920 --> 17:08.170
Why the hell aren't they reacting?

17:08.170 --> 17:10.590
They look like they're 
waiting for instructions,

17:10.590 --> 17:13.260
but the commander here has been captured.

17:13.260 --> 17:16.720
True, that's what Director Scorching said.

17:16.720 --> 17:20.020
Maybe the captured commander is a 
fake, so we'd let down our guard

17:20.020 --> 17:23.770
while they build up their strength here, 
and attack the village all at once.

17:23.770 --> 17:26.320
That would certainly explain the situation.

17:26.320 --> 17:29.150
Hold on, listen.
I've thought of a good plan.

17:31.150 --> 17:32.160
Here goes!

17:44.210 --> 17:46.090
<i>Good, all according to plan!</i>

17:46.090 --> 17:50.590
<i>What happened is, Hevee used his illusions 
to make them think their buddies are us.</i>

17:56.100 --> 17:58.600
I'm going to give this gear a little test.

17:58.600 --> 18:01.810
Become heavier!

18:03.390 --> 18:04.900
I did it!

18:04.900 --> 18:06.520
It looks like this will work.

18:13.110 --> 18:16.950
Looks like Field will be able to 
save up quite a bit of power.

18:16.950 --> 18:18.990
The problem is yet to come.

18:18.990 --> 18:22.620
The thing to do is charge forward while 
watching out for ambushes and traps.

18:22.620 --> 18:24.620
Could you be up front, Boxxo?

18:24.620 --> 18:26.960
We can probably prevent most 
of it with your barrier.

18:26.960 --> 18:28.420
<i>Y-ea, y-ea.</i>

18:28.420 --> 18:30.130
I'll go too then!

18:30.130 --> 18:33.800
Um, I'm sorry to interrupt.

18:33.800 --> 18:35.970
But can I get some extra food?

18:35.970 --> 18:37.470
I'm hungry.

18:40.060 --> 18:43.480
Boxxo, I think we'd better 
be cautious from here on.

18:43.480 --> 18:44.890
<i>Hello there.</i>

18:45.270 --> 18:46.560
Let's go.

18:56.200 --> 18:57.990
We made it!

18:58.530 --> 19:00.540
Everyone, you can come on!

19:04.620 --> 19:06.670
What's wrong, Hulemy?

19:06.670 --> 19:08.960
I was just thinking that if 
the ones who set these traps

19:08.960 --> 19:11.920
knew what we were doing 
to them, they'd be upset.

19:11.920 --> 19:15.680
<i>True. I think I'd be speechless if 
I were the one in charge of traps.</i>

19:15.680 --> 19:18.680
The enemies appear to be behind that door.

19:18.680 --> 19:21.850
All right. Lammis, go nuts on it.

19:21.850 --> 19:23.810
Okay, here goes!

19:26.270 --> 19:27.900
<i>Looks like they were lurking behind the door</i>

19:27.900 --> 19:30.520
<i>so they could pounce on 
us the second it opened,</i>

19:30.520 --> 19:33.030
<i>but that's only if you open 
it in a predictable way.</i>

19:33.860 --> 19:36.200
<i>They must be the Billowing Flames.</i>

19:37.410 --> 19:39.660
Who the hell're you guys?

19:39.660 --> 19:40.870
<i>That man...</i>

19:40.870 --> 19:43.750
<i>He matches the description 
we were given for Tashtay.</i>

19:43.750 --> 19:45.540
<i>That's got to be him!</i>

19:45.540 --> 19:49.040
We're hunters from Clearflow Lake stratum.

19:49.330 --> 19:52.500
What're you doing here,
if you're from another stratum?

19:52.960 --> 19:57.970
We're here because we have a little 
business to discuss with you,

19:58.510 --> 20:01.800
but we received more of a 
welcome than we expected.

20:02.100 --> 20:03.850
Business?

20:03.850 --> 20:09.310
Where the hell'd you find out we were hidin' 
monsters so we could go attack the village?

20:09.310 --> 20:11.940
<i>Sure enough, they were planning 
on attacking the village.</i>

20:12.440 --> 20:15.940
Would you mind answering my questions?

20:15.940 --> 20:17.070
Huh?

20:17.070 --> 20:19.990
Your group was conspiring with the Netherlord

20:19.990 --> 20:24.240
to attack the village using the 
monsters on the first floor.

20:24.240 --> 20:27.040
Is that accurate?

20:27.040 --> 20:31.500
If you know that much, there's no 
point in playing dumb anymore.

20:31.500 --> 20:32.840
Yeah, that's right.

20:32.840 --> 20:34.880
It's temporary, but we're working with him.

20:34.880 --> 20:37.130
Why're you on the Demon Lord's side?

20:37.130 --> 20:38.880
It's causing problems for everyone!

20:38.880 --> 20:42.760
Oh sure, thanks for your good-girl opinion.

20:42.760 --> 20:44.560
For money, that's why.

20:44.560 --> 20:48.390
Of course I'll do it, if I'm given enough 
money that I never have to work again.

20:48.390 --> 20:54.020
Have you long been in the habit of 
doing illegal things for money?

20:54.020 --> 20:55.980
Sure, you bet.

20:55.980 --> 21:00.200
Robbery? Rape? Beating clients to 
death? I've done my share of those.

21:00.200 --> 21:02.660
I was even a bandit, for a while.

21:02.990 --> 21:07.750
You wouldn't believe how great it 
feels to trample all over weaklings!

21:07.750 --> 21:09.370
Right, guys?

21:08.870 --> 21:10.290
It's the best!

21:10.290 --> 21:12.420
<i>These guys are total scum!</i>

21:12.420 --> 21:13.880
I see.

21:14.380 --> 21:17.920
Do you recognize these boots, then?

21:17.920 --> 21:19.760
What're they supposed to be?

21:19.760 --> 21:24.180
Tashtay, ain't those the boots we managed 
to sell recently for a high price?

21:24.180 --> 21:28.060
Oh yeah! The boots I stole 
from a hunter way back.

21:28.060 --> 21:29.680
Now I remember.

21:29.930 --> 21:33.230
That chick had the nerve to 
say she'd never hand 'em over,

21:33.230 --> 21:35.690
because she got 'em from 
someone dear to her.

21:35.690 --> 21:38.940
It pissed me off, so I cut 
off her freakin' legs.

21:39.860 --> 21:42.740
I see. At last...

21:44.070 --> 21:46.830
Looks like I get to achieve my goal.

21:46.830 --> 21:54.500
I've longed for this moment for years, 
and now it sneaks up on me so abruptly.

21:54.920 --> 21:57.000
You might cry and beg for forgiveness.

21:57.000 --> 21:58.800
You might cry out in intense pain.

21:58.800 --> 22:01.170
You might attempt to repent.

22:02.760 --> 22:04.970
But I will surely kill you.

23:35.020 --> 23:37.060
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

23:35.020 --> 23:40.020
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.020 --> 23:40.020
<b>Blizzard in the Desert</b>

23:37.940 --> 23:40.020
<i>I look forward to your next use.</i>
